{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Progress: plan review certified after one BLOCK (the draft left a temporary `fetched` branch that the bare clone would copy, keeping pre-reclaim history reachable; the plan now deletes it and the harness fails if the fake remote ever holds a branch other than tickets). Claimed. Implemented test-first on branch s8dc4-dry-run, commit 8b2466a9f80: src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_dry_run.py plus tests/unit/test_reclaim_dry_run.py (4 tests: happy path, no eligible boundary, non-empty workdir, CLI exit code). lint and typecheck green. make verify is running. The real-data dry run is running in a TMPDIR workdir with GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES set; it reads origin/tickets by a fetch of its resolved commit and publishes only to a file:// fake remote inside that workdir."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794886487403449981,"uuid":"c1a7a9d4-29ac-4913-b934-f906c5317a72"}